From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: response cursor for more than two duelists

Priority windows, simultaneous trigger order and phase-change windows now work when n_duelists > 2.
Before this, a 3 or 4 duelist duel hung when seat 1 ended its turn (the phase window asked only the
turn player and opponent_of(turn player)).

New helpers in field.h and field.cpp: response_order, first_responder, next_responder,
restart_responders, trigger_order, next_trigger_player. All skip eliminated duelists. New unit members:
QuickEffect::check_cursor, PhaseEvent::check_cursor and pass_count, PointEvent::conti_cursor.

Changed sites (every one is an if(n_duelists == 2) stock else new branch, or a guard that is false at n == 2):
- 6 sites where a Chain Link is added and the answer round starts: PhaseEvent step 2, QuickEffect step 1
  and step 3, IdleCommand, BattleCommand, ActivateEffect. n > 2 uses restart_responders(link owner).
- QuickEffect pass (step 3): next_responder at n > 2. Step 2: a duelist who is eliminated is not asked.
- QuickEffect steps 0 and 1: forced quick effects walk the trigger order with check_cursor.
- PointEvent step 9: first_responder of the open window or of the last Chain Link.
- PointEvent steps 30 to 33 (continuous free-chain effects): conti_cursor walks the trigger order.
- PointEvent SEGOC steps 3 and 6 (forced and optional triggers): next_trigger_player.
- PhaseEvent steps 0, 2 and 22: check_cursor and pass_count replace is_opponent and priority_passed.
- Phase changes in IdleCommand and BattleCommand: HINT_EVENT to every living duelist but the turn
  player, then the round starts after the turn player (who counts as passed).
- check_hint_timing, the TIMING_ATTACK test and the hint timing in MSG_SELECT_CHAIN (playerop.cpp)
  use the timings of the whole team and of all opponents at n > 2.

With 2 duelists every stock statement is unchanged and runs in the same order: no new message, no new
Lua call, no new random call. INVERTED_QUICK_PRIORITY is not used at n > 2.
Left for other tasks: battle, losses, elimination and zones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
